[The Trade Marks Rules, 2017 | CHAPTER I | Section 2 Definitions. (k)]
(k)  "graphical representation" means the representation  of a trademark for goods or services represented o r
capable of being represented in paper form and includes representation in  digitised form;

[The Trade Marks Rules, 2017 | CHAPTER I | Section 2 Definitions. (l)]
(l)  "Journal" means the trademarks Journal made available at official website of Controller General of Patents,
Designs and Trade Marks;

[The Trade Marks Rules, 2017 | CHAPTER I | Section 2 Definitions. (n)]
(n)   "old law" means the Trade and Merchandise Marks Ac t, 1958 and  rules made there under existing
immediately before the commencement of the Act;

[The Trade Marks Rules, 2017 | CHAPTER I | Section 2 Definitions. (q)]
(q)  "publish" means published in the trademarks Journal  made available on the official website of Controll er
General of Patents, Designs and Trademarks;

[The Trade Marks Rules, 2017 | CHAPTER I | Section 2 Definitions. (r)]
(r)  "registered trademark agent" means a trademark agen t whose name is actually on the register of
trademarks agents maintained under rule 142;

[The Trade Marks Rules, 2017 | CHAPTER I | Section 2 Definitions. (s)]
(s)  "renewal" means and includes renewal of registratio n of a trademark, certification trademark or collec tive
trademark, as the case may be;

[The Trade Marks Rules, 2017 | CHAPTER I | Section 2 Definitions. (w)]
(w)  "specification" means the designation of goods or s ervices in respect of which a trademark  or a regis tered
user of a trademark is registered or proposed to be registered;

[The Trade Marks Rules, 2017 | CHAPTER I | Section 4 Appropriate office of the Trade Marks Registry . (i)]
(i)  the principal place of business in India of th e registered proprietor of the trademark as entered  in the
register at such date is situate;

[The Trade Marks Rules, 2017 | CHAPTER I | Section 4 Appropriate office of the Trade Marks Registry . (ii)]
(ii)  where there is no entry in the register as to  the principal place of business in India of the re gistered
proprietor, the place mentioned in the address for service in India as entered in the register at such date is situate;

[The Trade Marks Rules, 2017 | CHAPTER I | Section 4 Appropriate office of the Trade Marks Registry . (iii)]
(iii) in the case of jointly registered proprietors , the principal place of business in India of the p roprietor
whose name is entered first in the register as having such place of business in India at such date is situate;

[The Trade Marks Rules, 2017 | CHAPTER II | Section 23 Form and signing of application. (a)]
(a) explain with sufficient precision, a descriptio n by words, of the trademark, if necessary, to dete rmine the
